Keep the menu opaque when the gradient carries alpha

The popup menu paints its background in the replacing composition mode.
The path first fills the rectangle of the menu with an opaque brush of
the palette, because a menu background gradient can carry alpha. The next
call covers the same rectangle in the same mode, so the fill reaches no
pixel of the render. A gradient with alpha therefore gives a translucent
menu, although the menu opacity option holds one hundred.

The path now leaves the replacing mode after the fill. The background
blends over the fill, so the menu keeps the opacity that the option
states. A menu opacity below one hundred takes no fill and keeps the
replacing mode, so a translucent menu does not move.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 6 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp
index d45c001d..dc48ea43 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve_primitive.cpp
@@ -1295,6 +1295,8 @@ Style::drawPrimitivePanelMenu(PrimitiveElement, const QStyleOption *option,
     // colour - this makes it consistent with Gtk.
     if (opts.menuBgndOpacity == 100) {
         painter->fillRect(r, option->palette.brush(QPalette::Window));
+        // The background blends over that fill, which keeps the menu opaque.
+        painter->setCompositionMode(QPainter::CompositionMode_SourceOver);
     }
     drawBackground(painter, bgCols[ORIGINAL_SHADE], r,
                    opts.menuBgndOpacity, BGND_MENU, opts.menuBgndAppearance);
